{"id":"wat-xieng-thong","name":"Wat Xieng Thong","qid":"Q2671118","country":"Laos","locality":"Luang Prabang","lat":"19.8975","lon":"102.143055555","built":"1560","year":1560,"year_text":"1560","century":"16th century","era":"Early modern","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"","heritage":"","type":"wat","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wat_Xieng_Thong","text":"Wat Xieng Thong (Lao: ວັດຊຽງທອງ, pronounced [wāt síaŋ.tʰɔ́ːŋ]; \"Temple of the Golden City\") is a Buddhist temple (vat or wat) on the northern tip of the peninsula of Luang Prabang, Laos. Built between 1559 and 1560 by King Setthathirath, Wat Xieng Thong is one of the most important of Lao monasteries and remains a significant monument to the spirit of religion, royalty and traditional art.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wat_Xieng_Thong","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-4216f05bfaab","w":1200,"h":714,"title":"Temple Wat Xieng Thong - Luang Prabang - Laos.jpg","o":"gh-4216f05bfaab.jpg","credit":{"text":"Basile Morin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Temple_Wat_Xieng_Thong_-_Luang_Prabang_-_Laos.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-69317217125f","w":1200,"h":751,"title":"Wat Xieng Thong Laos I.jpg","o":"gh-69317217125f.jpg","credit":{"text":"Phillip Maiwald ( Nikopol )","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wat_Xieng_Thong_Laos_I.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"civilization-vii--wat-xieng-thong","game":"civilization-vii","name":"Wat Xieng Thong","verified":false,"text":"","text_source":"","text_license":"","images":[{"id":"gh-p9f2167e61bf","w":1200,"h":675,"o":"gh-p9f2167e61bf.png","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Civilization VII, © 2K.","source":"https://civilization.fandom.com/wiki/File:Wat_Xieng_Thong_in-game_(Civ7).p